00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.550
I get it. You can find
beauty in anything, for sure.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.850
But also, you know,
there's a nice alignment

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.650
to things that feels good.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.720
And you know, when things are,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.303
when things are where
you expect them to be,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.817
doesn't that feel better?

00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:49.050
Okay. All right, carcinisation.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:49.890
I learned about this recently.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.310
This is a strange and
odd but funny phenomenon

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.140
and evolutionary biology where a bunch

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.410
of undersea crustaceans have
all slowly evolved towards

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.220
the same, flat, robust, crab-like shape

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.590
because it seems to be
the ideal form factor

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:05.910
for surviving in the ocean.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.830
Oversimplified, it feels
like everything down there is

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.050
evolving towards a crab.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.060
And look at all these crabs,

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.850
lots of smartphones today
basically look the same.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.090
So when something that comes
along looks a little different,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.070
well it's gonna feel weird, isn't it?

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.740
But hey, maybe someone's
into the layered glass look

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.990
with the text in various places.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.060
Maybe you're into the
red dot turning into a

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.380
functional record light.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.330
Maybe you're into a bit of a lobster.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.340
Real talk though, it feels
like every few months Nothing

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.107
comes out with a new
product that looks crazy

00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:35.940
and people hate on all the pictures

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.350
on the internet 'cause they look weird.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.450
And then two months later
we're all used to it

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.860
and we forget about the looks

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.040
and we can focus on the product itself.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.940
So let's just skip all that
and focus on the product.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.170
This is what Nothing is calling
their first true flagship,

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.970
which is what you would
say if you're Nothing

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:58.170
and you're charging $799 for a
phone for the first time ever

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.790
after rolling around in the budget

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.530
and mid-range space for a few years.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.030
But I've been using this
phone for the better part

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.310
of the last week and I'm gonna disagree

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.620
with the whole premise here actually.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.556
This is no more of a
flagship phone than any

00:02:10.556 --> 00:02:14.100
of Nothing's previous phones.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.300
Now are they lying to us?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:21.180
Eh, not exactly but kind of. Hear me out.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.290
799 is the same price
as a Samsung Galaxy S25

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.620
or the Pixel 9, or right
underneath the iPhone 16.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.160
Like they're competing against
bonafide flagships from mega

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.320
companies with basically unlimited money.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.570
And part of what we've come
to expect from phones in this

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:40.740
class is basically giving
us the best available stuff.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.810
Like it's kind of this unspoken rule,

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.440
but if you're spending
this much, you deserve

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.770
to just get the best parts, right?

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.820
That's why it's been so easy for me

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.713
to rag on like the Pixel in the past

00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:52.470
for not having the best performance

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.350
or the iPhone for not having
a high refresh rate display.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.330
So this Nothing Phone 3,

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.040
it's certainly dressed up like a flagship

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.040
and it is the most flagship
yet of any Nothing phone.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:02.873
It is huge.

00:03:02.873 --> 00:03:06.600
It's got this super bright,
high refresh rate, OLED display.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.390
It has a massive new
silicon carbon battery,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.500
new triple 50 megapixel
cameras, IP 68 certification,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.000
up to 16 gigs of RAM.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.700
Like it's got all the makings
of what could be a flagship.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.680
But when you peel back the
mask, just a little bit,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.640
like right under the surface,
it's the same exact strategy

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.170
that Nothing has been running on all their

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.580
previous phones in the past.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:27.600
The playbook is

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.540
to just cut back just a little
bit from the highest end

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.160
stuff in ways that hopefully
you, the buyer, don't notice.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.810
And it still feels like a flagship,

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.490
but that allows 'em to cut costs

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.980
and undercut the competition a little bit.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.870
So it works. It's not a bad strategy.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.450
It's allowed 'em to make
great phones in the past,

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.210
but it's just harder to sell
that strategy at this price.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.250
So for starters, the chip inside, right?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.070
It's not the expensive,
proven, powerful flagship

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.810
Snapdragon 8 Elite chip.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.530
This is running the
Snapdragon 8s Gen 4 instead.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.420
It's one of the first phones
we've seen using this chip.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:04.590
And to be fair, it is much
better than anything we've seen

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.240
in any previous Nothing phone.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.740
It's a four nanometer chip,

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.290
it's something like 40% better CPU

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.485
and like 90% better GPU than
the chip in the two year-old

00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:14.760
Nothing Phone 2.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.250
The phone is zippy and smooth as hell,

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.300
basically all the time.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.010
And I'll get to the software
experience in a second.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.820
But is it the best available?
Well, technically no.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.010
The Snapdragon 8 Elite still smokes this.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.780
You can see benchmark
scores, it's pretty clear

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.730
that's still the flagship chip.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.880
Now you as the user
might never notice that.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.220
In fact you probably wouldn't
if you just used the phone

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.740
side by side in a lot of
random, normal activities.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.340
But if you happen to get into
graphically intensive gaming

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.060
or the most intense tasks,
that's what separates a flagship

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.350
from an upper mid-range chip.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.450
So for some context, some
other phones using this chip,

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.787
the Poco F7 and the Iqoo Neo 10,

00:04:51.787 --> 00:04:54.240
both of these are sub $500 phones.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.010
I also think they were
very clever pairing it up

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:59.850
with 12 gigs of RAM and
256 gigs of storage base.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.481
It's fast Ram, it's UFS 4.0

00:05:01.481 --> 00:05:05.220
and then the upgraded
version for 899 is 16 gigs

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.410
of RAM and half a terabyte.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.519
Awesome to see that. But
there is no 8 128 version.

00:05:10.519 --> 00:05:12.272
And I think if they did make one,

00:05:12.272 --> 00:05:15.600
that would probably be
like 699, but they didn't.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.060
Now when we get to the outside
of this phone, there is this,

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.550
again, huge new AMOLED display.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.440
Surely it's a flagship display, right?

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.280
It's gigantic.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.458
It's 6.67 inches corner to corner

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:28.140
with perfectly even
bezels all the way around,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.430
that takes extra work.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.295
It's a gorgeous AMOLED,
nice color reproduction

00:05:32.295 --> 00:05:34.620
and it's also, it's a
good amount over 1080P.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.420
It's nice and sharp, smooth

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.912
with that dynamic refresh
rate up to 120 hertz

00:05:38.912 --> 00:05:42.510
and it gets crazy bright,
1600 nits outdoors,

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:45.600
4,500 nits peak brightness with HDR.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.961
So the numbers on paper go crazy

00:05:46.961 --> 00:05:49.680
and it's just, it's such
a nice screen to look at.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.373
I've loved using it. So
what's the catch, Marques?

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.270
Well one, you would
literally never know this

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.290
unless you check the spec sheet,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.350
but the glass protecting
the front of this display,

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.330
it's Gorilla Glass 7i,

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.400
and that is a mid-range
glass in their lineup

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.441
where you might see flagships
using the more durable

00:06:06.441 --> 00:06:10.650
Gorilla Glass Victus or Victus 2.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:11.910
And normally I wouldn't even bring that up

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.830
but that's definitely something
to consider on a phone

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.710
that is meant to spend a
lot of its time face down.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.420
And then another thing, there are a lot

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.610
of like really nice, subtle
things that go into this screen.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.710
Like it has a 1,000
hertz touch sample rate,

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.810
so it's even more responsive
than the phone too.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.720
It also has 2160 hertz PWM dimming

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.210
and it also has a very acceptable
optical fingerprint reader

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.251
down near the bottom.

00:06:31.251 --> 00:06:33.720
But it's also an LTPS display,

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:35.577
instead of the most premium LTPO.

00:06:35.577 --> 00:06:37.800
And all that really means
in practice is instead

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.040
of varying a refresh rate
from one to 120 hertz,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.980
it can go from 30 to 120 hertz.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.890
You would never notice, but
it does mean a little bit

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.120
worse power efficiency.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.332
I'll tell you what though, it
can actually absolutely handle

00:06:50.332 --> 00:06:51.165
the slightly worse power efficiency

00:06:51.165 --> 00:06:54.360
because the battery in
this phone is elite.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:57.720
It's marketed as a 5100
50 milliamp power battery,

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.060
but according to Nothing
and it gets complicated

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.780
but it's actually rated at a
5,500 milliamp power battery.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:07.770
It's silicon carbon, it
charges extra fast at 65 watts.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.140
It supports wireless charging,
reverse wireless charging,

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.407
reverse wired charging.

00:07:11.407 --> 00:07:12.570
It's great.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.640
It sips power in standby

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.890
and it's genuinely a two day
phone if you want it to be,

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.050
even without the more
efficient Snapdragon 8 Elite.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.026
So honestly flagship battery for sure.

00:07:21.026 --> 00:07:24.240
So then, okay, what about the cameras?

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.240
Triple 50 megapixel cameras
feels pretty flagship.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.050
And you know what, again, it is closer

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.970
to a flagship than any previous

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.890
Nothing phone has ever been,

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.300
but I've used this now for a little bit.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:40.260
It's still a notch behind
the S25's and Pixel 9's

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.610
and iPhone 16's of the world.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.040
The mainstream flagships
that I'm comparing this to.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.470
This main sensor is the
biggest they've ever used,

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:47.790
one over 1.3 inches.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:51.210
It lets a ton more light in
and I'm shooting with this

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:52.560
and I realize as I'm looking

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.420
through all the pictures I've taken,

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.660
for some reason it's frequently soft.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.550
Like even on a perfectly normal shot,

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.869
the colors will be fine,
the exposure will be fine,

00:08:01.869 --> 00:08:04.852
but the subject of the
photo when I zoom in,

00:08:04.852 --> 00:08:08.700
it should be in sharp focus
but it's just a little bit off.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.610
I think you can blame this
a little bit on auto focus,

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:14.130
maybe a little bit on
tuning for a larger sensor

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.810
with shallower depth of field.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.580
It's definitely capable of good pictures

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.904
and it's a little bit wider
than you might expect,

00:08:19.904 --> 00:08:22.530
but yeah, that's a little bit odd.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:26.610
Then the telephoto is 3x, also
a tiny bit soft sometimes,

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.690
but also very useful.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.190
It's where your macro shots come from

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:32.090
and you can get some really
sick, impressive closeups

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:34.320
and the ultra wide and the selfie cameras,

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.440
they are the most consistent
and most flagship of them all.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.730
But yeah, like I said,

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:41.340
the whole camera setup is just one notch

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:42.960
behind those things.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.910
And you may only notice
if you're zooming in

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.350
and pixel peeping.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:48.000
But again, that's the point.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.390
Mostly good enough for most
people, most of the time.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:53.730
I think with a little tuning,
this can be an A minus camera.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.580
I think a perfect
encapsulation of the priorities

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.730
of this phone are, I mean
look at, look at this design.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:03.150
It's an insane design but
technically no camera bump.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.310
I mean the rings obviously
protrude a little bit,

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.337
but most flagship phones at
this point also have some sort

00:09:08.337 --> 00:09:11.430
of big camera bump that they all sit on.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:14.495
It turns out to get this
whole big telephoto camera

00:09:14.495 --> 00:09:18.390
to not have a bump that actually
engineered part of the PCV

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.790
or the board inside to have a hole in it.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.640
So the optics could
actually split like punch

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.170
through the PCB instead

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.300
of being stacked totally on top of it.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.040
I'm sure we'll see this in
like a JerryRigEverything

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.330
tear down video at some point.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.630
But yeah, basically mission
accomplished, no camera bump,

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:34.890
but that also meant they had

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:37.200
to use some smaller parts to make it work.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.440
And this is actually a
physically smaller telephoto

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.960
than the cheaper Nothing Phone 3a Pro.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.950
So spoiler, the design
is still the priority

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.563
of this phone, always has been.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.070
But let's talk about the
most controversial bit

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.260
of this design, which is the glyphs,

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.970
which made Nothing Phones famous

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.650
for a couple years.

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:01.740
This year, the glyph lights are gone

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.920
and replacing them is this
small display on the back

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:06.180
upper corner of the phone.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.918
It's 489 LED pixels.

00:10:08.918 --> 00:10:11.670
They're calling it Glyph Matrix.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:16.670
On its face, this has
some usefulness about it,

00:10:16.795 --> 00:10:20.340
but then it's also surrounded by gimmicks.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.100
Okay, so the basic idea is
like your phone is face down

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.540
and then the lights on
the back would light up

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.776
and you could tell something
about what that notification is

00:10:26.776 --> 00:10:30.450
to decide if you wanna actually
pick it up and check or not.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:33.570
So if that is all you're after, then okay,

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.720
success, you know, more
pixels means more information.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.960
The new essential
notifications builder is super

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.640
powerful and informative.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.110
It's better than ever before.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:46.590
I can set up a certain
icon to come up in the dots

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.930
whenever I get a certain
type of notification

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.790
or anything from a certain person

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.200
or from a certain app.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.420
Let's say I wanna be able
to leave my phone face down,

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:58.140
but I never wanna miss any
notifications from Mom, ever.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.280
Okay, set that up.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.130
No matter what she sends,
no matter how she sends it,

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:04.920
I will get an icon or a
picture from my gallery

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.650
or something that it can
turn into dots and done.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:09.210
Anytime mom calls or texts

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:11.340
or whatever, I can't see what they said,

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.380
but I can see that she sent me something.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.630
So that's convenient, that's functional.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:16.800
Outside of that,

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.824
it immediately starts feeling
way more gimmicky, like, okay,

00:11:20.824 --> 00:11:23.550
take another look at the back
of this phone, you see a,

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.160
you see this little dot
here hidden in this design?

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:30.060
This little circle is actually
a pressure sensitive area.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.940
And when you press that,
the back display lights up

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.400
and then you can use a
single press to cycle

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.100
through these glyph toys

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.890
and then a long press to
actually engage with them.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.060
So you can cycle to a timer

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.935
and then start a timer on
the back of your phone,

00:11:44.935 --> 00:11:48.210
which doesn't sync up
with the actual clock app.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.700
So if you turn your phone
screen on the timer disappears.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.200
So be careful.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.510
You can also use the back display

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:58.890
as a viewfinder for your
main camera kind of,

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:00.480
or you can play spin the bottle.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:01.313
Maybe you're into that.

00:12:01.313 --> 00:12:03.630
Maybe you and your friends
don't have a bottle handy,

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.670
but you have your Nothing phone.

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:08.490
Or you can play Rock, Paper, Scissors

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.380
against your own phone.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.990
I think you get the idea.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:15.840
They're fun tech demos, but the
utility runs out real quick.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:17.640
Now they have opened up the API.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.710
So developers, if they want to,

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:23.040
can make more stuff for the back screen.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.480
I, you know, with this
phone, I don't really know

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:26.100
how many actually will, like,

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.920
is Spotify gonna make like album art,

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.715
cover art on the back of the phone here?

00:12:31.715 --> 00:12:32.610
I don't know.

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:35.010
But the Nothing community has
already started developing

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.570
some stuff and messing with it.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.270
They've made this one.
This is a magic eight ball.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.860
So instead of turning your phone over

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.177
and asking Google for a magic eight ball,

00:12:43.177 --> 00:12:45.210
you can ask the back of your phone

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:47.580
and it'll give you a little message.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:48.413
Cool.

00:12:48.413 --> 00:12:49.891
Look, the real best part

00:12:49.891 --> 00:12:54.450
of a Nothing phone is still
the software on the front

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.940
of the phone because Nothing OS 3.5,

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.060
soon to be updated to
4.0, it's just great.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:02.430
Like they have this tastefully modified

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:04.628
version of Android with
this nice aesthetic,

00:13:04.628 --> 00:13:07.260
finely-tuned, smooth performance

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.120
and a handful of useful features

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.890
that they just sort of sprinkle in there.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.033
So you can sort of choose
which ones you want to use

00:13:13.033 --> 00:13:14.610
or easily ignore.

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.730
The AI-powered essential
space continues to evolve

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.110
and get more features, though it doesn't

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.340
sync with anything externally.

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.630
So I don't use it.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.160
And yes, there's still a custom button

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.360
for it on the side of the phone,

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.620
but it's not too in-your-face.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.600
You can ignore it if
you don't wanna use it.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.640
And the little things like being able

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.800
to resize the quick settings toggles

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.410
or the way you can swipe up
on the camera app to flip

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.600
through presets, which is so clean.

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.973
Everything is, it's clean,
it's smoothly animated

00:13:38.973 --> 00:13:41.700
and the whole OS is responsive in ways

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:45.120
that feel higher end than
the specs would ever suggest.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:48.240
I think the best new
feature on this phone is

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.410
the universal search box.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.880
So you might actually
kind of get it confused

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.730
'cause there's a permanent
Google search box on the bottom

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.200
of the home screen at all times.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.083
Not that search box,

00:13:56.083 --> 00:13:59.610
but when you pull up the
app drawer, that search box.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.670
Now, that one searches through
your stuff on your phone,

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.488
like usual, or you can ask it a question

00:14:05.488 --> 00:14:07.560
and hit that AI button

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:10.380
and it'll use a modified
version of Gemini to go online

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:12.690
and pull up a short and
sweet answer for you.

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:14.199
It's tuned to kind of just be brief

00:14:14.199 --> 00:14:16.210
and give you answers to stuff.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.160
It's nice.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.587
And again, you can choose to use it

00:14:18.587 --> 00:14:21.300
or just never even try.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.770
You can just leave it tucked away

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.540
and it's just, you can use
it the way you normally do

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.260
and just search for
your apps on your phone.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:27.987
And this is also gonna get updates.

00:14:27.987 --> 00:14:31.470
They are gonna do, they're
promising five years

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.030
of major software updates.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.260
I could do the nitpicky thing

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.450
and be like, oh, Samsung's
doing seven years

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:37.590
and Apple does even more.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:38.790
So it's not quite a flagship,

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.740
but you've seen how flagships kind

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.760
of vary all over the board.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:44.190
So I'm giving them flagship
credit for the software.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.620
So at the end of the day, is the title

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:50.280
of this review a little dramatic maybe?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.870
Sure.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:56.870
But flagship, the word flagship
is being used here heavily

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.548
as a marketing term.

00:14:58.548 --> 00:15:00.630
And so maybe the review title

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.593
should just been Nothing Phone 3,

00:15:02.593 --> 00:15:04.740
They Did Marketing, whatever.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.960
But the point is, it still stands.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.240
They're charging 799 for this phone

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:10.740
and there are other really good phones

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.450
that you can get for that much money.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:16.500
So this phone, just like previous
Nothing Phones is the one

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.300
that you would get if you really care,

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:22.620
not so much about raw specs,
but about good software

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:23.943
and a unique design.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:28.353
You don't want another
crab, you want lobster.

00:15:29.276 --> 00:15:32.340
Thanks for watching. Catch
you guys the next one.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:33.430
Peace.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.513
(funky upbeat music)

